      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I forgot I was running SteamVR beta (to fix an unrelated memory leak when using a different headset). Unfortunately this only complicates matters even more, because the issues with VRC are different depending if I'm on live or beta SteamVR.\n\nTest results as of today:\n\n- **SVR live, VRC live** - no problems, works the way it always did\n\n- **SVR live, VRC beta** - hand position is correct, but fingers are stuck in a default resting position and no finger tracking works at all, regardless of legacy fingers setting\n\n- **SVR beta, VRC live** - no problems, works the way it always did\n\n- **SVR beta, VRC beta** - same problem as in original video\n\nThere are no problems in any case in SteamVR Home both live and beta, although I'm not sure that's a valid test for this issue, as the hands there appear to only use simple position/rotation and grip strength. The ghost controllers in the SVR loading grid work fine too, and show correct data for touchpad thumb position, thumbstick position, trigger position, etc.\n\nSince I was running SVR beta for all prior skeletal input testing, I do not know if this worked on SVR live in pre-1487 VRC open beta.\n\nIf there's anything else I can test please let me know.\n\ncc @{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name}",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
